@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il28-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Row IL-28: the taxpayers and the readings the tests use, generated by tools/gen_people.py.
-- Every field of every taxpayer is spelled out. No expected value is here: they are in the tests modules,
-- written by hand from the Hebrew text before the code was run.
--
-- Lettering of the readings: A is the first reading listed under the fork in ito-il28-nouns.l4 and NOTES.md,
-- B the second, D the declined default. FW2 has no B.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `The taxpayers`

`an Area man` MEANS Taxpayer WITH
    `the tax year`                                            IS 2025
    `an individual`                                           IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                                 IS FALSE
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                     IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area`                                  IS TRUE
    `an Israeli citizen under the Citizenship Law`            IS FALSE
    `entitled to immigrate under the Law of Return`           IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer's residence in the Area over the tax year`  IS `the Area residence entered held for the whole tax year`
    `a favoured individual within section 37`                 IS FALSE
    `the spouse's livelihood was upon the taxpayer`           IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer proved it to the assessor's satisfaction`   IS FALSE
    `the taxpayer had income from personal exertion in the tax year` IS TRUE
    `a worker`                                                IS FALSE
    `a resident of Israel within the Foreign Workers Law`     IS FALSE
    `holds a visa under section 2 of the Entry into Israel Law, or needs one` IS FALSE
    `stay in Israel or the Area and employment there are permitted by law` IS FALSE
    `an expert from abroad or a guest lecturer`               IS FALSE
    `holds a B/1 temporary worker visa and licence`           IS FALSE
    `holds a permit to work in the caring sector`             IS FALSE
    `the stay is extended under section 3A(b) of the Entry into Israel Law` IS FALSE
    `the months of the tax year spent in Israel or the Area`  IS 12
    `the income taxed is income under section 2(1) or (2)`    IS TRUE

